# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of the checking-out
# machine's core.autocrlf setting. A CRLF line ending inside `set -euo
# pipefail` (or any bash control-flow line) breaks parsing outright —
# confirmed as a real failure mode (see the git log around the
# test_dispatch_worktree.py fixture fix).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Python/JS tolerate either line ending at runtime, so this pin is pure
# hygiene (clean diffs, no autocrlf-induced churn on Windows checkouts) —
# not a correctness fix like the *.sh rule above.
*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf

# --- H-D: repo line-ending policy (specs/PACK_HARDENING_2026-08.md §4) ---
#
# ORCH decision on spec §8 Q1: option (b) — `* text=auto` going forward only,
# WITHOUT a mass renormalization commit (option (a) would have been a single
# large whitespace-only diff touching every tracked text file). This is the
# lower-risk choice for a pack other projects sync from byte-exactly: do NOT
# run `git add --renormalize .` / `git diff --renormalize` and commit the
# result on top of this file — that would rewrite tracked-file bytes wholesale
# and is exactly what this policy was chosen to avoid. Existing files are left
# as-is until they are next touched; new/edited text files get LF normalized
# into the repository automatically from here on.
#
# Interaction with scripts/sync_from_pack.py: sync's entire conflict model is
# hash equality over byte-exact reads (read_bytes/write_bytes, no encoding or
# newline translation — see the CRLF lesson noted in that script's own
# docstring) comparing the pack's on-disk working-tree bytes against each
# downstream project's copy. That comparison happens on disk, not through a
# fresh `git checkout`, so this policy does not by itself flip clean files to
# CONFLICT. A bulk renormalization commit WOULD, because it changes the bytes
# every downstream project's baseline is compared against — which is the
# second reason option (b) was chosen over (a).
#
# `*.md text eol=lf` targets PLAN.md specifically: `* text=auto` alone still
# lets core.autocrlf convert LF blobs to CRLF on checkout (Windows), which is
# what produced the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every PLAN.md
# edit; the explicit eol=lf pins the working-tree line ending so the warning
# stops. PLAN.md's stored content is already LF, so this does not change any
# committed bytes.
* text=auto
*.md text eol=lf

# Explicit binary markings — none of these extensions are tracked in this
# repo today, but pin them now so a future addition (screenshots in specs/,
# vendored fonts, a bundled sqlite fixture, etc.) never gets text-normalized
# or line-ending-converted by accident.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.bundle binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
